**Add `--json` in `cli.js` only.** No change to `report.js` or `format.js`.

```js
const json = argv.includes('--json');
const rows = buildRows();
process.stdout.write((json ? JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2) : toTable(rows)) + '\n');
```

One call to make. [`toTable`](src/format.js:14) drops `owner` and `slow`. [`buildRows`](src/report.js:11) keeps both. I would print all six fields as JSON. Say so if you want just the four table columns.
